  "step_3": "The decision reason requires comparing the probability of the maximum outcome: Lottery A has a 45% chance of 6000 Euros (the maximum), while Lottery B has a 0% chance of 6000 Euros (since it only offers up to 3000 Euros). Thus, the reason would prefer Lottery A. However, the individual's verbal report does not mention the maximum outcome or its probability. Instead, the individual justifies the choice based on the risk factor (90-10), indicating a focus on the probability of a non-zero outcome rather than the likelihood of the highest possible payoff. Since the individual neither considers the probability of the maximum outcome nor applies the rule of preferring the lottery with the higher probability of the maximum outcome, the decision reason was not used. The individual’s reasoning is based on a different criterion (risk profile), not the one specified in the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
